e/ecommerce/e2e/ShopUnderTest.java src/test-e2e/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/e2e/ProviderPaymentE2ETest.java src/test-e2e/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/e2e/pages/ReviewPage.java; cat src/main/resources/templates/checkout/review.pug; cat .agents/factory/decisions/*.md; sed -n '/## Look and feel/,/## Not part/p' project/product.md","description":"Read tests, template, decision, product"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WFnTmVYZLRK8Sis3MKseLg","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java; grep -rn 'new PaymentResult\\|PaymentResult(' src | grep -v 'shared/PaymentProvider.java'; cat src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/checkout/infrastructure/CheckoutDomainConfiguration.java; grep -rn 'ConditionalOn' src/main/java | head -5; ls ~/.gradle/caches/modules-2/files-2.1/org.springframework.boot/ | grep -i 'restclient\\|http-client'","description":"More call-site checks"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_014rroyGy8ZWEu56ZQCkjqcM","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java; f=$(ls build/test-results/test-integration/*ProviderPayment*.xml); grep -A15 \"<failure\" $f | head -40","description":"Show failure details"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XwKokGdgMANoExjmYPULz9","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/checkout/adapter/outgoing/payment/RestPaymentProvider.java'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    } catch (final RestClientException e) {\n      return''','''    } catch (final RestClientException e) {\n      LOG.warn(\"Payment request for checkout session {} failed\", sessionId.value(), e);\n      return''')\ns=s.replace('''                if (!response.getStatusCode().isSameCodeAs(HttpStatus.CREATED)) {\n''','''                if (!response.getStatusCode().isSameCodeAs(HttpStatus.CREATED)) {\n                  LOG.warn(\n                      \"Payment provider answered {} for checkout session {}\",\n                      response.getStatusCode(),\n                      sessionId.value());\n''')\ns=s.replace('''  private static final String NOT_IN_CONTRACT''','''  private static final Logger LOG = LoggerFactory.getLogger(RestPaymentProvider.class);\n  private static final String NOT_IN_CONTRACT''')\ns=s.replace('import org.springframework.boot','import org.slf4j.Logger;\\nimport org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;\\nimport org.springframework.boot',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"value()\" src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/checkout/domain/model/CheckoutSessionId.java | head -3","description":"Add warning logs to adapter"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KR33ANg9tsoWC5iT4r76zR","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java; head -4 build/test-results/test-e2e/TEST-dev.domaincentric.sample.ecommerce.e2e.ProviderPaymentE2ETest.xml; ./gradlew spotlessCheck -q 2>&1 | grep -v WARNING; echo rc=$?; git status --short","timeout":300000,"description":"Check e2e result, format, status"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":53,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The build stage for `pay-through-the-provider` is finished and all three acceptance criteria now pass. Every suite the profile declares ran and passed, including `ProviderPaymentIntegrationTest` (4/4) and `ProviderPaymentE2ETest` (1/1). The notes are in `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/build.md`. Nothing is committed.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Payment result:** `PaymentResult` now has three outcomes: succeeded, refused, and unavailable (new). `SubmitPaymentUseCase` raises the existing `PaymentProviderUnavailableException` when the provider is unavailable.\n- **New REST adapter (`RestPaymentProvider`):** it sends `POST /payments` with the amount and currency and gives up after 2 seconds.\n  - `201` with a reference means authorized, `402` means refused.\n  - A timeout, a connection failure or any other status counts as unavailable, and is logged as a warning.\n  - It is only switched on when `checkout.payment-provider.base-url` is set. Otherwise the existing stand-in (`MockPaymentProvider`) takes payments, so a local run still needs no provider.\n- **Payment page:** `PaymentPageController` now shows the story's two exact messages for a refused payment and an unavailable provider.\n- **Review page:** the total now has `data-test=\"review-total\"` so the browser test can read it.\n- **Context map:** the payment provider declaration in `checkout/package-info.java` now describes the REST adapter with the stand-in as fallback. `docs/architecture/context-map.md` was regenerated from it, not edited by hand.\n\n**Deviations from the plan, both recorded in `build.md`:**\n- **New config class:** I added `CheckoutPaymentConfiguration` so Spring picks up the new provider-address setting. The project has no automatic scan for settings classes, and this follows the existing `JwtProperties` / `SecurityConfiguration` pair.\n- **HTTP/1.1 only:** I pinned the HTTP client to HTTP/1.1. The JDK client tries to switch to HTTP/2 by default, and the test stub cut the connection on the `402`. That made a refused payment show the \"not available\" message, and the refused test failed until I changed it.\n\n**For the document stage:** the JavaDoc of `PaymentInitiationFailedException` still says the customer sees the provider's reason. The page no longer shows it. I left the JavaDoc unchanged because the plan didn't list that class.\n\nI checked every file I wrote against `dca-discipline`. I did not consult `dca-knowledge`, because the plan had already settled every pattern question.","ttft_ms":2590,"type":"result","duration_ms":497242,"uuid":"10c11211-6c2f-4070-b1c9-9d35f12271d9","ttft_stream_ms":1698,"time_to_request_ms":41,"first_content_frame_ms":1698,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
